---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/region';
---

<Base
  title={`Request removal of a listing | ${SITE.shortName}`}
  description="Ask Base Impact to remove your organization from our resource guide. No reason required — we remove it."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 py-16">
    <h1 class="mb-4 text-4xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">
      Request removal of a listing
    </h1>

    <p class="mb-8 text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
      <strong>If your organization is listed on this site and you want it removed, we will remove
      it. No reason required.</strong> You do not have to explain why. A listing is a courtesy, not
      something we hold over you.
    </p>

    <div class="mb-10 rounded-2xl border border-emerald-200 bg-emerald-50 p-6 dark:border-emerald-800 dark:bg-emerald-950/40">
      <p class="mb-2 font-bold text-emerald-900 dark:text-emerald-200">What happens next</p>
      <ol class="list-decimal space-y-1 pl-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-emerald-900 dark:text-emerald-200">
        <li>We acknowledge your request within <strong>2 business days</strong>.</li>
        <li>We remove or hide the listing within <strong>5 business days</strong> — sooner if you ask urgently.</li>
        <li>We record the request so the listing cannot reappear in a future update.</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-emerald-900 dark:text-emerald-200">
        We may tell you once if we think the listing is useful to the community. You still decide.
        Your decision is final.
      </p>
    </div>

    <section class="mb-10 space-y-6 text-slate-700 leading-relaxed dark:text-slate-300">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">Fastest: email us</h2>
      <p>
        Send an email to{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}?subject=Removal%20request`} class="font-semibold text-emerald-800 underline dark:text-emerald-400">
          {SITE.email}
        </a>{' '}
        with the subject line <strong>&ldquo;Removal request&rdquo;</strong>. Include the
        organization name and, if you can, the page you saw it on. That is all we need.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">Or use the form</h2>
      <p>
        The same form we use for corrections and suggestions works for removals — just choose
        <strong>&ldquo;Remove my organization&rdquo;</strong> in the reason field.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a
          href="/submit"
          class="inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-emerald-800 px-6 py-3 font-semibold text-white transition-colors hover:bg-emerald-900"
        >
          Open the form
        </a>
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">Corrections welcome too</h2>
      <p>
        If you would rather stay listed but something is wrong — wrong phone number, wrong hours, a
        service you no longer offer — tell us and we will fix it from your own website. Many
        organizations prefer this, and it is usually faster than removal.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">Why we do this</h2>
      <p>
        A directory that will not remove a listing on request is publishing information about
        someone without their consent. We are a small local nonprofit and we have no interest in
        doing that. If you want out, you are out.
      </p>
    </section>

    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-6 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-700 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-300">
      <p class="mb-1 font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">Questions about how we list?</p>
      <p>
        Our <a href="/sources" class="underline">Sources page</a> shows where each listing came
        from, and our full listing policy is published in the site repository.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
